WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.372
Some problems cannot be safely fixed automatically.

00:00:03.372 --> 00:00:09.937
A negative price should not automatically become positive unless we know the intended value.

00:00:09.937 --> 00:00:16.742
A bad date string should not be replaced with today's date simply to avoid a missing value.

00:00:16.742 --> 00:00:22.597
A missing phone number should not be filled using some unrelated contact field.

00:00:22.597 --> 00:00:28.216
And a possible duplicate should not be deleted simply because it has a lower identifier.

00:00:28.918 --> 00:00:35.775
The safer response is often to preserve the source, produce a cleaned value only when justified,

00:00:35.775 --> 00:00:37.860
and add a review status.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:44.045
This may feel less satisfying because the dataset still contains unresolved problems.

00:00:44.045 --> 00:00:46.670
But that is actually more honest.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:51.935
A clean dataset should not mean a dataset where uncertainty has been hidden.

00:00:51.935 --> 00:00:59.707
It should mean a dataset where known transformations are consistent and unresolved uncertainty is clearly represented.
